  "definition": "An Earth observation sensor is the functional system that carries out an observing procedure and produces a result about a property of the Earth, its oceans or its atmosphere. The term can denote a detector element, a physical sensing assembly or a wider observing system, depending on context. ESA's glossary uses it broadly for an instrument or device that collects data, while formal metrology and semantic standards draw different boundaries.[^1]",
